# Raw input: Ultra-high-resolution photograph capturing the majestic Grand Teton Range in Ansel Adams' iconic black-and-white aesthetic, rendered with extreme detail and dynamic range. The composition centers on the sharp, snow-capped peaks of the Teton Crest, dramatically silhouetted against a vast sky filled with textured, wispy cirrus clouds. Sunlight, likely during the golden hour, sculpts the granite faces with deep, velvety shadows and luminous highlights, revealing intricate rock striations, glacial scarring, and subtle texture in the snowfields. Below, the pristine, glassy surface of Jackson Lake mirrors the peaks with near-perfect clarity, capturing ripples and reflections in extreme fidelity. The mood is profound, timeless, and awe-inspiring, evoking the raw power of nature. Colors are desaturated to near-monochrome, emphasizing profound blacks, silvery grays, and pure whites, with subtle hints of cool blue in the shadows and warm gold in the illuminated snow. Visible textures include the rough, pitted stone of the cliffs, the smooth, almost liquid surface of the lake, and the delicate, feathery clouds. Shot on film simulation with a large-format camera perspective, featuring sharp focus throughout the scene, deep depth of field, and Adams' signature high-contrast tonal range. Quality tags: 8K resolution, photorealistic, cinematic, ultra-detailed textures, film grain simulation, dramatic lighting, natural landscape photography, timeless composition, sharp focus, rich blacks, luminous highlights, cinematic atmosphere, 16mm film aesthetic.
